{
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**The task.** Return all elements of a matrix in spiral order — top row left to right, right column downward, bottom row right to left, left column upward, then inward and repeat."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Example"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "text",
      "code": "[[1, 2, 3],\n [4, 5, 6],      ->   [1,2,3,6,9,8,7,4,5]\n [7, 8, 9]]"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "The approach"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Four boundaries. Walk one edge, then pull that boundary inward. Stop when the boundaries cross."
    },
    {
